(prd002-sys R1, R2)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys/ component description, technology choices, DD3)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (full requirements and type definitions for pkg/sys/)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc003-sys.yaml (sys foundation use case)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (existing golang.org/x/sys/unix usage for TIOCGWINSZ -- reference pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo.go\n        action: create\n        note: Portable file metadata type and Lstat wrapper function\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go\n        action: create\n        note: Darwin-specific Stat_t field extraction (Mtimespec, Blocks)\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go\n        action: create\n        note: Linux-specific Stat_t field extraction (Mtim, Blocks)\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal.go\n        action: create\n        note: TerminalSize query via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement a portable file metadata type wrapping os.FileInfo that exposes modification time and disk block count extracted from the platform-specific syscall.Stat_t, abstracting Mtimespec (Darwin) vs Mtim (Linux) per prd002-sys R1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement an Lstat function returning the portable metadata type for symlink-aware stat so callers never import platform-specific packages per prd002-sys R1\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement a TerminalSize function returning (columns int, rows int, err error) via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl using golang.org/x/sys/unix per prd002-sys R2\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Isolate all platform-specific Stat_t field access in build-tagged files (_darwin.go and _linux.go) so the portable API compiles cleanly on both platforms per prd002-sys design decisions\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"golang.org/x/sys/unix is the only external dependency -- use it for IoctlGetWinsize and Stat_t field access (architecture technology choices section)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Platform-divergent code in _darwin.go and _linux.go with //go:build tags; portable API in fileinfo.go and terminal.go (architecture DD3: common logic promoted to pkg/)\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"pkg/sys/ is the sole import point for golang.org/x/sys/unix -- cmd/ packages use pkg/sys/ and never import golang.org/x/sys directly (architecture technology choices: 'pkg/sys wraps this into a single internal API')\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo.go defines the portable metadata type with access to modification time and block count, plus an Lstat wrapper\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go extracts modification time and blocks from Darwin syscall.Stat_t using Mtimespec\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go extracts modification time and blocks from Linux syscall.Stat_t using Mtim\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"pkg/sys/terminal.go exports TerminalSize returning columns, rows, and error\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/ passes with no diagnostics on the build platform\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19443,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19443},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e094eb49-7aef-4b96-8eda-f48c6dc292a1","uuid":"5ef2e7da-5aaf-418f-86c8-6f34c6956fe9"}
