{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":287305,"duration_api_ms":287241,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge from reference behavior on edge cases, flag interactions, and exit codes. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go binaries), `pkg/sys/` (Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (specifications).\n\n**Current state**: `pkg/format/` has source code on this branch (color.go, column.go, size.go). All other packages have specs complete but no code on the working branch. Generated code from prior pipeline runs exists only at generation-merged tags.\n\n**Current release**: Release 00.0 (Foundation) with four use cases:\n- uc001-magefiles — spec complete, code not started (magefiles/ excluded; cmd/version/ is valid target)\n- uc002-format — spec complete, **code already exists** (skip)\n- uc003-sys — spec complete, code not started\n- uc004-testutils — spec complete, code not started\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 has three remaining code targets: `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/testutils/`, and `cmd/version/`. Per P8 (libraries before consumers), the two `pkg/` libraries come before `cmd/version/`. Between `pkg/sys/` and `pkg/testutils/`, both are independent shared libraries — neither consumes the other. Alphabetical tie-breaking (P8): `pkg/sys/` < `pkg/testutils/`. Therefore `pkg/sys/` is the first task.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/sys/ file metadata and terminal size (prd002-sys R1, R2)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys/ component description, technology choices, DD3)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (full requirements and type definitions for pkg/sys/)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc003-sys.yaml (sys foundation use case)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (existing golang.org/x/sys/unix usage for TIOCGWINSZ -- reference pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo.go\n        action: create\n        note: Portable file metadata type and Lstat wrapper function\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go\n        action: create\n        note: Darwin-specific Stat_t field extraction (Mtimespec, Blocks)\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go\n        action: create\n        note: Linux-specific Stat_t field extraction (Mtim, Blocks)\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal.go\n        action: create\n        note: TerminalSize query via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement a portable file metadata type wrapping os.FileInfo that exposes modification time and disk block count extracted from the platform-specific syscall.Stat_t, abstracting Mtimespec (Darwin) vs Mtim (Linux) per prd002-sys R1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement an Lstat function returning the portable metadata type for symlink-aware stat so callers never import platform-specific packages per prd002-sys R1\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement a TerminalSize function returning (columns int, rows int, err error) via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl using golang.org/x/sys/unix per prd002-sys R2\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Isolate all platform-specific Stat_t field access in build-tagged files (_darwin.go and _linux.go) so the portable API compiles cleanly on both platforms per prd002-sys design decisions\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"golang.org/x/sys/unix is the only external dependency -- use it for IoctlGetWinsize and Stat_t field access (architecture technology choices section)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Platform-divergent code in _darwin.go and _linux.go with //go:build tags; portable API in fileinfo.go and terminal.go (architecture DD3: common logic promoted to pkg/)\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"pkg/sys/ is the sole import point for golang.org/x/sys/unix -- cmd/ packages use pkg/sys/ and never import golang.org/x/sys directly (architecture technology choices: 'pkg/sys wraps this into a single internal API')\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo.go defines the portable metadata type with access to modification time and block count, plus an Lstat wrapper\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go extracts modification time and blocks from Darwin syscall.Stat_t using Mtimespec\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go extracts modification time and blocks from Linux syscall.Stat_t using Mtim\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"pkg/sys/terminal.go exports TerminalSize returning columns, rows, and error\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/ passes with no diagnostics on the build platform\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"e094eb49-7aef-4b96-8eda-f48c6dc292a1","total_cost_usd":0.54162475,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19443,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"output_tokens":16418,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19443,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":16418,"cacheReadInputTokens":19292,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19443,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.54162475,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"76f5fa1b-daaa-4eb5-aff6-dcfb93cb4dc4"}
